tgs:Human.SimonMichaux a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:prefLabel "Simon Michaux"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Associate Professor of Geometallurgy, Geological Survey of Finland (GTK), Circular Economy Solutions Unit. PhD in Mining Engineering (JKMRC, University of Queensland). 18 years in the Australian mining industry before moving to Belgium (University of Liège) and then Finland to research industrial recycling and the circular economy. Author of the widely-cited 2021 GTK report 'Restructuring the Circular Economy into the Resource Balanced Economy,' arguing existing green-transition mineral-supply plans are logistically impractical at proposed scale. No independent Wikipedia/DBpedia page found — confirmed real via GTK's own staff page, Google Scholar (897+ citations), and his own site."@en ;
    .

tgs:Human.PedroPrieto a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:prefLabel "Pedro Prieto"@en ;
    owl:sameAs <https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pedro_Prieto> ;
    rdfs:comment "Telecom engineer (30 years, ITT R&D Labs and Alcatel) turned solar-energy analyst. Vice president and co-founder of AEREN (Asociación para el Estudio de los Recursos Energéticos), which represents ASPO (Association for the Study of Peak Oil and Gas) in Spain; board member of ASPO International. Led several real solar PV installations in Spain since 2004. Co-author with Charles A. S. Hall (a real, notable EROI researcher and Odum student already referenced elsewhere in this graph via Concept.MaximumPowerPrinciple) of 'Spain's Photovoltaic Revolution: The Energy Return on Investment' (2013) — the first complete real-world EROI energy analysis of a large-scale PV deployment, finding real EROI too low to seamlessly support an energy transition."@en ;
    .

